    "description": "What: a crew's switches, asked by triggers (CE-4670, vehicle appearance VA-3 / VA-4; docs/designs/vehicle-appearance/DESIGN_Vehicle_Appearance_State.md §6a / §6b). On basic-desert at 00:30 local, a T-72 and an M109 howitzer (whose seats hold its crew: driver, gunner, commander) idle 200 m apart: 'Lit Tank' at (550, 250) under Normal discipline, 'Blacked-out Howitzer' at (550, 450) authored Blackout. At 5 s a trigger switches the Lit Tank to Blackout (SetVehicleLights) and puts the Blacked-out Howitzer's commander's head out of his hatch (HeadOut, role Commander); at 10 s another switches the Blacked-out Howitzer to Convoy. Judge: the Lit Tank is lit (head + tail, OnMask 3) until the switch, then dark with its discipline Blackout; the Blacked-out Howitzer's commander's hatch (its first opening) opens and stays open with the crewman exposed to the end, its driver's hatch never opens; under Convoy it shows only the convoy marker (group 3, OnMask 8). Fail: a switch that does not change the lights, a hatch that closes while he is out, or a wrong hatch.",
